        "geoBonBiome": [
          "Terrestrial"
        ],
        "geology": "Durzon is composed of karstified carbonates of the Jurassic. Two thick series can be found on this causse: the series of the Hettangian (from a total power from 50 to 300 m) and the series from Dogger to Malm (with a total power up to 600 m). These two series are separated by a marl series (black and laminated marls) deposited at the Domérien and Toarcien. They play an important role in the hydrology of the Duzon by constituting respectively a waterproof barrier and base.\r\n",
        "hydrology": "Located at an altitude of 533m, the source of the Durzon will deliver an average discharge of 1.5 m3/s over the period 2008 to 2014. The min discharge may reach 0.7 m3/s as in the summer 2011 and the max discharge may reach until 16 m3/s.\r\nThe bassin area is estimated between 98 and 117 km2 depending on the authors and based on a mass bilan.\r\nOverflows of many of the surrounding epikarst aquifers during extreme events can lead to the formation of temporary lakes.",
        "soils": "Soil depth is too heterogeneous in our karstic site to provide one parameters and we do not have a complete map. All the parameters of the soil are not well adapted to our site.",
        "vegetation": "The vegetation is essentially reduced to low grass, with low transpiration and shallow setting"
      },
